@prefix triage: <urn:atm:triage:> .
@prefix xsd: <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .

triage:PhaseAY a triage:Phase .

# Order follows the plan's execution waves (docs/plans/phase-ay/phase-ay-plan.md,
# "Sprint map, parallel tracks and stacking"). Wave 1: AY.1 (docs, standalone) and
# AY.2 (stack bottom) in parallel. Linear gh stack: AY.2 -> AY.3 -> AY.4 -> AY.5 -> AY.6 -> AY.7.
# AY.8 is a standalone join gated on AY.1+AY.2+AY.3 merged and P-E(b); AY.9 is the last
# sprint, gated on AY.7+AY.8 merged. The cursor does not encode the wave gates; the
# orchestrator checks must_follow merges (and P-E rulings for AY.3/AY.8) before dispatch.
# Stack linking: gh stack link needs two args, so the stack is created on AY.3's first push
# (gh stack link --base integrate/phase-ay 1269 feature/ay3-...; AY.2 is PR #1269) rather than AY.2's first
# push (GitHub refuses zero-commit PRs), then `gh stack link <stack#> feature/ayN-...` per
# subsequent sprint push. Never gh stack rebase/sync/merge; merge commits only.
triage:AY1 a triage:Sprint ; triage:inPhase triage:PhaseAY ; triage:order 1 ; triage:branch "feature/ay1-herdr-audit-docs" ; triage:criteria "docs/plans/phase-ay/sprint-AY.1-herdr-audit-docs.md" .
